{"version": "6.9", "hitCount": 3, "request": {"queryString": "\"KRT23\" AND \"lacrimal gland\"", "resultType": "core", "cursorMark": "*", "pageSize": 8, "sort": "", "synonym": false}, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "35216421", "source": "MED", "pmid": "35216421", "pmcid": "PMC8875482", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC8875482"]}, "doi": "10.3390/ijms23042307", "title": "Comparison of Different Mass Spectrometry Workflows for the Proteomic Analysis of Tear Fluid.", "authorString": "Jones G, Lee TJ, Glass J, Rountree G, Ulrich L, Estes A, Sezer M, Zhi W, Sharma S, Sharma A.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Jones G", "lastName": "Jones", "firstName": "Garrett", "initials": "G", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lee TJ", "lastName": "Lee", "firstName": "Tae Jin", "initials": "TJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5245-1140"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Glass J", "lastName": "Glass", "firstName": "Joshua", "initials": "J", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Rountree G", "lastName": "Rountree", "firstName": "Grace", "initials": "G", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Ulrich L", "lastName": "Ulrich", "firstName": "Lane", "initials": "L", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Estes A", "lastName": "Estes", "firstName": "Amy", "initials": "A", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Sezer M", "lastName": "Sezer", "firstName": "Mary", "initials": "M", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Zhi W", "lastName": "Zhi", "firstName": "Wenbo", "initials": "W", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Sharma S", "lastName": "Sharma", "firstName": "Shruti", "initials": "S", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Sharma A", "lastName": "Sharma", "firstName": "Ashok", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9597-4374"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Population Health Sciences, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8200-108X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9597-4374"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5245-1140"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data", "related_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "4", "volume": "23", "journalIssueId": 3318866, "dateOfPublication": "2022 Feb", "monthOfPublication": 2, "yearOfPublication": 2022, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci", "title": "International journal of molecular sciences", "essn": "1422-0067", "issn": "1422-0067", "nlmid": "101092791", "isoabbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci"}, "printPublicationDate": "2022-02-01"}, "pubYear": "2022", "pageInfo": "2307", "abstractText": "The tear film is a multi-layer fluid that covers the corneal and conjunctival epithelia of the eye and provides lubrication, nutrients, and protection from the outside environment. Tear fluid contains a high concentration of proteins and has thus been recognized as a potential source of biomarkers for ocular disorders due to its proximity to disease sites on the ocular surface and the non-invasive nature of its collection. This is particularly true in the case of dry eye disease, which directly impacts the tear film and its components. Proteomic analysis of tear fluid is challenging mainly due to the wide dynamic range of proteins and the small sample volumes. However, recent advancements in mass spectrometry have revolutionized the field of proteomics enabling unprecedented depth, speed, and accuracy, even with small sample volumes. In this study using the Orbitrap Fusion Tribrid mass spectrometer, we compared four different mass spectrometry workflows for the proteomic analysis of tear fluid collected via Schirmer strips. We were able to establish a method of in-strip protein digestion that identified >3000 proteins in human tear samples from 11 healthy subjects. Our method offers a significant improvement in the number of proteins identified compared to previously reported methods without pooling samples.", "affiliation": "Center for Biotechnology and Genomic Medicine, Medical College of Georgia, Augusta University, Augusta, GA 30912, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "National Eye Institute", "grantId": "P30 EY031631", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NEI NIH HHS", "acronym": "EY", "grantId": "P30 EY031631", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Eye Institute", "grantId": "R01 EY029728", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Tears", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "CH", "qualifierName": "chemistry"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Dry Eye Syndromes", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Eye Proteins", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Proteomics", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Adult"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Middle Aged"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Female"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Male"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Mass Spectrometry", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Young Adult"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Workflow"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Biomarkers", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Mass spectrometry", "Proteomics", "Biomarkers", "Ocular Surface", "tear film", "Dry Eye Disease"]}, "chemicalList": {"chemical": [{"name": "Eye Proteins", "registryNumber": "0"}, {"name": "Biomarkers", "registryNumber": "0"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Unpaywall", "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/1422-0067/23/4/2307/pdf?version=1645263275"}, {"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms23042307"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8875482"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC8875482?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 34, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "Y", "dbCrossReferenceList": {"dbName": ["PRIDE"]}, "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "Y", "license": "cc by", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "Y", "tmAccessionTypeList": {"accessionType": ["go", "uniprot", "doi"]}, "dateOfCompletion": "2022-03-22", "dateOfCreation": "2022-02-26", "dateOfRevision": "2024-04-09", "electronicPublicationDate": "2022-02-19", "firstPublicationDate": "2022-02-19", "firstIndexDate": "2022-02-27", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2025-02-02", "hasEvaluations": "N"}, {"id": "34769520", "source": "MED", "pmid": "34769520", "pmcid": "PMC8584501", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC8584501"]}, "doi": "10.3390/ijms222112090", "title": "Transcriptome Analysis of Pterygium and Pinguecula Reveals Evidence of Genomic Instability Associated with Chronic Inflammation.", "authorString": "Suarez MF, Echenique J, L\u00f3pez JM, Medina E, Ir\u00f3s M, Serra HM, Fini ME.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Suarez MF", "lastName": "Suarez", "firstName": "Mar\u00eda Fernanda", "initials": "MF", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5519-9286"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "New England Eye Center, Tufts Medical Center and Department of Ophthalmology, Tufts University School of Medicine, Boston, MA 02111, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Echenique J", "lastName": "Echenique", "firstName": "Jos\u00e9", "initials": "J", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2638-0577"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Centro de Investigaciones en Bioqu\u00edmica Cl\u00ednica e Inmunolog\u00eda (CIBICI), Department of Clinical Biochemistry, Faculty of Chemistry, National University of C\u00f3rdoba, C\u00f3rdoba 5000, Argentina."}]}}, {"fullName": "L\u00f3pez JM", "lastName": "L\u00f3pez", "firstName": "Juan Manuel", "initials": "JM", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8481-5834"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Instituto de Microcirug\u00eda Ocular C\u00f3rdoba (IMOC), C\u00f3rdoba 5000, Argentina."}]}}, {"fullName": "Medina E", "lastName": "Medina", "firstName": "Esteban", "initials": "E", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Instituto de Microcirug\u00eda Ocular C\u00f3rdoba (IMOC), C\u00f3rdoba 5000, Argentina."}]}}, {"fullName": "Ir\u00f3s M", "lastName": "Ir\u00f3s", "firstName": "Mariano", "initials": "M", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Instituto de Microcirug\u00eda Ocular C\u00f3rdoba (IMOC), C\u00f3rdoba 5000, Argentina."}]}}, {"fullName": "Serra HM", "lastName": "Serra", "firstName": "Horacio M", "initials": "HM", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4979-8642"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Centro de Investigaciones en Bioqu\u00edmica Cl\u00ednica e Inmunolog\u00eda (CIBICI), Department of Clinical Biochemistry, Faculty of Chemistry, National University of C\u00f3rdoba, C\u00f3rdoba 5000, Argentina."}]}}, {"fullName": "Fini ME", "lastName": "Fini", "firstName": "M Elizabeth", "initials": "ME", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "New England Eye Center, Tufts Medical Center and Department of Ophthalmology, Tufts University School of Medicine, Boston, MA 02111, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Programs in Cell, Molecular & Developmental Biology and Pharmacology & Drug Development, Tufts Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences, Boston, MA 02111, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5519-9286"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8481-5834"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2638-0577"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4979-8642"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data", "related_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "21", "volume": "22", "journalIssueId": 3257605, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Nov", "monthOfPublication": 11, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci", "title": "International journal of molecular sciences", "essn": "1422-0067", "issn": "1422-0067", "nlmid": "101092791", "isoabbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-11-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "12090", "abstractText": "Solar damage due to ultraviolet radiation (UVR) is implicated in the development of two proliferative lesions of the ocular surface: pterygium and pinguecula. Pterygium and pinguecula specimens were collected, along with adjacent healthy conjunctiva specimens. RNA was extracted and sequenced. Pairwise comparisons were made of differentially expressed genes (DEGs). Computational methods were used for analysis. Transcripts from 18,630 genes were identified. Comparison of two subgroups of pterygium specimens uncovered evidence of genomic instability associated with inflammation and the immune response; these changes were also observed in pinguecula, but to a lesser extent. Among the top DEGs were four genes encoding tumor suppressors that were downregulated in pterygium: <i>C10orf90</i>, <i>RARRES1</i>, <i>DMBT1</i> and <i>SCGB3A1</i>; <i>C10orf90</i> and <i>RARRES1</i> were also downregulated in pinguecula. Ingenuity Pathway Analysis overwhelmingly linked DEGs to cancer for both lesions; however, both lesions are clearly still benign, as evidenced by the expression of other genes indicating their well-differentiated and non-invasive character. Pathways for epithelial cell proliferation were identified that distinguish the two lesions, as well as genes encoding specific pathway components. Upregulated DEGs common to both lesions, including <i>KRT9</i> and <i>TRPV3</i>, provide a further insight into pathophysiology. Our findings suggest that pterygium and pinguecula, while benign lesions, are both on the pathological pathway towards neoplastic transformation.", "affiliation": "New England Eye Center, Tufts Medical Center and Department of Ophthalmology, Tufts University School of Medicine, Boston, MA 02111, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIH HHS", "acronym": "NH", "grantId": "R01EY026479", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "R01EY026479", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NEI NIH HHS", "acronym": "EY", "grantId": "R01 EY026479", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Argentina National Agency for Scientific and Technological Promotion", "grantId": "PICT 2016-0055", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Research to Prevent Blindness", "grantId": "none", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Massachusetts Lions Eye Research Fund", "grantId": "none", "orderIn": 0}]},